a calculation you currently repeat;
at least one figure or table; and
a clear reader and output format.

7.2 Add safeguards when they solve a problem
Possible next layers include:

Git for change history and collaboration;
renv for an R package lockfile;
automated rendering in continuous integration;
parameterised reports;
Quarto manuscripts and journal extensions;
project profiles for student and solution variants;
a shared institutional theme; and
publishing to an internal server or static host.

The Beyond the workshop appendix gives a starting point without making these tools prerequisites.

B.5 YAML parsing fails
Check:

spaces rather than tabs;
aligned indentation;
a colon after each key;
matching quotation marks; and
opening and closing --- lines.

Temporarily reduce the YAML to title and one format, render, then restore one option at a time.

B.9 Recovery route
If you fall behind:

save your current file with a different name;
copy the relevant .qmd from the completed project;
render it to rejoin the workshop; and
compare files after the session.
